# Who "an approving review" has to come from.
#
# Without this file the ruleset could only require *an* approval, which any
# account with write access could give — including another contributor
# approving a second contributor. Naming an owner for every path is what makes
# the requirement mean "the owner reviewed it".
#
# This does not gate the owner's own pull requests, and cannot: GitHub never
# lets anyone approve their own PR, so a sole owner bound by this rule could
# never merge anything. The review ruleset grants repository admins bypass for
# exactly that reason. The rules worth having against yourself — pull request
# required, `CI / green`, no force-push, no deletion — live in a separate
# ruleset with no bypass at all, so this exemption cannot reach them.

